IELTS.lesson({"test": 5, "part": 1, "title": "Test 5, Part 1 — the interview", "candidate": "hadi", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "Good morning. Come in, have a seat.", "ar": "صباح الخير. تفضّل بالدخول واجلس.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1b2def3fa2b0b362.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "My name is Mohamad Khorbatli. Can you tell me your full name, please?", "ar": "اسمي محمد خرباطلي. هل يمكنك أن تخبرني باسمك الكامل من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c756d0707f344069.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Hadi Mansour.", "ar": "هادي منصور.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/ceaffd822a91ae16.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "And what can I call you?", "ar": "وبماذا أناديك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/5085ae49113e09cf.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Hadi is fine.", "ar": "هادي يكفي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/5712e414c47baa37.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you, Hadi. Can I see your identification, please?", "ar": "شكراً لك يا هادي. هل يمكنني رؤية هويتك من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/766d885dd8bfeba2.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Of course. Here you are.", "ar": "بالتأكيد. تفضّل.", "shot": null, "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/9db6bd4d7b1e7b70.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That's all fine.", "ar": "شكراً. كل شيء على ما يرام.", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a65ff8d3eccec277.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now, in this first part I'd like to ask you some questions about yourself. Let's talk about transport.", "ar": "الآن، في هذا الجزء الأول أودّ أن أطرح عليك بعض الأسئلة عنك. لنتحدّث عن المواصلات.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c4d113ed9d21f34b.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How do you usually travel to work?", "ar": "كيف تذهب إلى عملك عادةً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/89237b45b404a170.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I drive. It's about forty minutes, maybe fifty if the Hama road is bad. I've got an old car. It's fine, it does the job.", "ar": "أقود سيّارتي. المسافة نحو أربعين دقيقة، وربّما خمسين إذا كان طريق حماة سيّئاً. عندي سيّارة قديمة. لا بأس بها، تؤدّي الغرض.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/c63149fe461218db.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you enjoy the journey?", "ar": "هل تستمتع بالطريق؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c4d06e789fc7da23.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "It's all right. I listen to the radio. To be honest the first twenty minutes on the Hama road are the best part of my day, because nobody can phone me and I don't have to answer anyone.", "ar": "لا بأس به. أستمع إلى الراديو. بصراحة، العشرون دقيقة الأولى على طريق حماة هي أفضل جزء من يومي، لأنّ لا أحد يستطيع أن يتّصل بي ولست مضطرّاً أن أجيب أحداً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/418f233a76c59e7a.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Has transport in your city improved?", "ar": "هل تحسّنت المواصلات في مدينتك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f141341fb0f1149e.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Yeah, it's better. The roads around Hama are better than they were, basically. There's more cars now so sometimes it's worse, but generally it's better. It's improved.", "ar": "نعم، صارت أفضل. الطرقات حول حماة أفضل مما كانت، أساساً. صار هناك سيّارات أكثر فأحياناً يكون الوضع أسوأ، لكن بشكل عام هو أفضل. لقد تحسّن.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/a51e0757e409b70e.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Would you prefer to use public transport?", "ar": "هل تفضّل استخدام النقل العام؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a7b0786d274a9aa7.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "No. I mean, if it was good, maybe. But it isn't, so no.", "ar": "لا. أعني، لو كان جيّداً فربّما. لكنّه ليس كذلك، فلا.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/f439df4439dedfd1.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's move on to talk about travelling in your country.", "ar": "لننتقل للحديث عن السفر داخل بلدك.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/efca6b7692b7692e.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Have you travelled much inside Syria?", "ar": "هل سافرت كثيراً داخل سوريا؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/82c86766a52a5679.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "A fair bit, yeah. Work takes me around, basically. Hama, Tartous once for three months, Damascus when I have to. Put it this way, I've seen more of it than I'd have chosen to.", "ar": "لا بأس، نعم. العمل يأخذني إلى أماكن كثيرة، أساساً. حماة، وطرطوس مرّة لثلاثة أشهر، ودمشق حين أضطرّ. لنقل إنّني رأيت منها أكثر مما كنت سأختار أن أرى.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/679b495fed011156.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Which part of the country do you like most?", "ar": "أيّ جزء من البلد تحبّ أكثر؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/8b3f7c31fa55c7b3.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "The coast. It's green, it's completely different, you come over the mountains and the air changes. My wife's family is from near Jableh so we go when we can.", "ar": "الساحل. أخضر، ومختلف تماماً، تعبر الجبال فيتغيّر الهواء. عائلة زوجتي من قرب جبلة فنذهب حين نستطيع.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/6e77f14f8e02fc49.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you think tourism will grow in your country?", "ar": "هل تظنّ أنّ السياحة ستنمو في بلدك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c9e437a8ccd7818d.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I think, yes, it'll grow. There's a lot of, of history here, a lot of places, the castles and the Old City in Damascus and this. So it could happen, I think it will grow, but it needs the, the situation to be stable, you know, for a long time. So it depends on that really.", "ar": "أظنّ، نعم، ستنمو. هناك كثير من، من التاريخ هنا، وأماكن كثيرة، القلاع والمدينة القديمة في دمشق وهذا. فقد يحصل ذلك، أظنّ أنّها ستنمو، لكن يحتاج الأمر إلى أن يكون، أن يكون الوضع مستقرّاً، تعرف، لمدّة طويلة. فالأمر يتوقّف على ذلك في الحقيقة.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/41dc1956b99ecee3.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Is it important for people to travel inside their own country?", "ar": "هل من المهمّ أن يسافر الناس داخل بلدهم؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/b15ed3f6047c6f68.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Yes, it's important. Because you understand the country better, I think. If you only know Hama, you don't know Syria. So it's important, yes.", "ar": "نعم، مهمّ. لأنّك تفهم البلد بشكل أفضل، في رأيي. إذا كنت تعرف حماة وحدها فأنت لا تعرف سوريا. فهو مهمّ، نعم.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/43d312c3d47d1e1a.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Finally in this part, let's talk about keeping fit.", "ar": "وأخيراً في هذا الجزء، لنتحدّث عن الحفاظ على اللياقة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/64d4d628d3857eb6.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you do any sport or exercise?", "ar": "هل تمارس أيّ رياضة أو تمارين؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/29855b5a83ba9379.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Football, Friday. That's it, really. My job is physical anyway. I'm walking six floors maybe fifteen times a day, so I don't feel guilty about not going to a gym.", "ar": "كرة قدم، يوم الجمعة. هذا كلّ شيء، فعلاً. عملي بدني على أيّ حال. أصعد ستّ طوابق نحو خمس عشرة مرّة في اليوم، فلا أشعر بالذنب لأنّني لا أذهب إلى النادي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/53aab968d00c80b0.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Is it easy to stay fit where you live?", "ar": "هل من السهل الحفاظ على اللياقة حيث تعيش؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/8e9ed24cb7cfc90d.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Easy enough if you're not fussy. There's no proper gym near me in Hama, but there's a pitch and there's the hill behind the house. To be honest the facilities aren't the problem. Everyone's just tired.", "ar": "سهل بما يكفي إن لم تكن صعب الإرضاء. لا يوجد نادٍ حقيقي قربي في حماة، لكن هناك ملعب وهناك التلّة خلف البيت. بصراحة، المرافق ليست هي المشكلة. الجميع متعبون فحسب.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/f741c366d2c99974.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Did you play sport when you were at school?", "ar": "هل كنت تمارس الرياضة حين كنت في المدرسة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/df9bc57c400e472d.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Same thing, basically. Football, badly. At school in Hama I was the one they put at the back because I wouldn't stop running. That's not a skill, that's just not being clever enough to stand still.", "ar": "الشيء نفسه، أساساً. كرة قدم، وبشكل سيّئ. في المدرسة في حماة كنت الذي يضعونه في الخلف لأنّني لا أتوقّف عن الركض. هذه ليست مهارة، هذه فقط أنّني لم أكن ذكيّاً بما يكفي لأقف مكاني.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/4c46783b12301b06.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you think young people are less active than they used to be?", "ar": "هل تظنّ أنّ الشباب أقلّ نشاطاً مما كانوا؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c07861e8c59b212c.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Probably, but I mean, where would they go? When I was a kid the street was the pitch. Now there are cars parked on it. It's easy to blame the children for something that's actually about parking.", "ar": "على الأرجح، لكن أعني، إلى أين يذهبون؟ حين كنت طفلاً كان الشارع هو الملعب. الآن هناك سيّارات متوقّفة فيه. من السهل أن تلوم الأطفال على شيء هو في الحقيقة عن مواقف السيّارات.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/e06d1bc272f2fe94.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of Part One.", "ar": "شكراً لك. بهذا ينتهي القسم الأول.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/50f379466faf1658.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "How do you usually travel to work?", "ar": null, "topic": "Transport", "model": "I drive. It's about forty minutes, maybe fifty if the Hama road is bad. I've got an old car. It's fine, it does the job.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "Answers in two words and adds exactly what the question asked for. The Hama road is the specific that makes it his drive and nobody else's."}, {"q": "Do you enjoy the journey?", "ar": null, "topic": "Transport", "model": "It's all right. I listen to the radio. To be honest the first twenty minutes on the Hama road are the best part of my day, because nobody can phone me and I don't have to answer anyone.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "A small, honest reason for liking something, and the real one. The best part of the day is defined by what does not happen in it."}, {"q": "Has transport in your city improved?", "ar": null, "topic": "Transport", "model": "Yeah, it's better. The roads around Hama are better than they were, basically. There's more cars now so sometimes it's worse, but generally it's better. It's improved.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "Concedes, qualifies, concedes again. Plain and completely clear, which is what band 7 actually sounds like."}, {"q": "Would you prefer to use public transport?", "ar": null, "topic": "Transport", "model": "No. I mean, if it was good, maybe. But it isn't, so no.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "A conditional, correctly formed — and then the answer stops. A band 7 answer would have given one reason. This gives none."}, {"q": "Have you travelled much inside Syria?", "ar": null, "topic": "Travelling in your country", "model": "A fair bit, yeah. Work takes me around, basically. Hama, Tartous once for three months, Damascus when I have to. Put it this way, I've seen more of it than I'd have chosen to.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "Three places and a date, then a dry line. 'more of it than I'd have chosen to' carries a whole working life in seven words."}, {"q": "Which part of the country do you like most?", "ar": null, "topic": "Travelling in your country", "model": "The coast. It's green, it's completely different, you come over the mountains and the air changes. My wife's family is from near Jableh so we go when we can.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "A sensory specific ('the air changes') and a reason. His best answer of the test."}, {"q": "Do you think tourism will grow in your country?", "ar": null, "topic": "Travelling in your country", "model": "I think, yes, it'll grow. There's a lot of, of history here, a lot of places, the castles and the Old City in Damascus and this. So it could happen, I think it will grow, but it needs the, the situation to be stable, you know, for a long time. So it depends on that really.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "Hesitates, restarts and still arrives somewhere. The condition at the end is the answer: it depends on stability."}, {"q": "Is it important for people to travel inside their own country?", "ar": null, "topic": "Travelling in your country", "model": "Yes, it's important. Because you understand the country better, I think. If you only know Hama, you don't know Syria. So it's important, yes.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "Hama against Syria is the whole argument, made with two place names and no abstraction."}, {"q": "Do you do any sport or exercise?", "ar": null, "topic": "Keeping fit", "model": "Football, Friday. That's it, really. My job is physical anyway. I'm walking six floors maybe fifteen times a day, so I don't feel guilty about not going to a gym.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "Two words, then the reason he does not need more. Six floors fifteen times is evidence."}, {"q": "Is it easy to stay fit where you live?", "ar": null, "topic": "Keeping fit", "model": "Easy enough if you're not fussy. There's no proper gym near me in Hama, but there's a pitch and there's the hill behind the house. To be honest the facilities aren't the problem. Everyone's just tired.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "Separates the excuse from the cause, and names the cause as tiredness rather than blaming anything."}, {"q": "Did you play sport when you were at school?", "ar": null, "topic": "Keeping fit", "model": "Same thing, basically. Football, badly. At school in Hama I was the one they put at the back because I wouldn't stop running. That's not a skill, that's just not being clever enough to stand still.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "Self-deprecation with a turn in it. 'clever enough to stand still' is his own joke about his own stamina."}, {"q": "Do you think young people are less active than they used to be?", "ar": null, "topic": "Keeping fit", "model": "Probably, but I mean, where would they go? When I was a kid the street was the pitch. Now there are cars parked on it. It's easy to blame the children for something that's actually about parking.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "A rhetorical question, a contrast with his own childhood, and a sharp closing line. This is the Hadi who scores 7.0 — compare it with his Part 3 answers in Test 5."}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120"}});
